  <!-- ============ 06 PATTERN ============ -->
  <section class="node-section shell" id="sec-6">
    <span class="node-index">06</span>
    <h2>The surface it all <em>sits on</em>.</h2>
    <p class="section-lede">
      A single tile, derived from the node joints in the wordmark, repeating without a
      visible seam. It gives a surface a quiet technical texture without adding a colour.
    </p>

    <div class="pattern-row">
      <div class="pattern-wrap">
        <div class="pattern-fill" role="img" aria-label="Seamless network pattern tile"></div>
        <span class="caption">Seamless tile · 420 px repeat</span>
      </div>
      <div class="pattern-side">
        <div class="pattern-fact">
          <h3>Tone on tone only</h3>
          <p>The tile lives inside one colour family, roughly 4–8 % apart from its ground.
             It should never be readable from across a room.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pattern-fact">
          <h3>Behind, never beside</h3>
          <p>It sits under content as a ground. It is not a graphic element and does not
             share a frame with the mark at equal contrast.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="pattern-fact">
          <h3>Scales with the surface</h3>
          <p>Large on vehicle and wall applications; small and near-invisible on screen —
